WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.840
 - Hello, and welcome to our security lecture.

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:05.520
 I'm Charles Severance, and I encourage

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.920
 you to grab the PowerPoints and remix them and use them

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:10.840
 in your own courses.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:11.680
 Use the videos.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.040
 Use everything in your own courses.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.000
 You don't have to teach this whole course.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.480
 It's quite a bit.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:22.680
 So let's start out by meeting some nice people.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:28.180
 These people are Alice and Bob, and they simply

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:31.320
 want to communicate some information left

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.260
 to their own devices.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:34.440
 And they don't want the rest of the world

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.140
 to know about what they're communicating,

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:39.440
 and so they want to encrypt it some way.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:44.680
 Now, in the cryptography world, they all

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:48.520
 call these two people, the good people, Alice and Bob.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:53.120
 And they simply are A and B, very computer-esque variable

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:55.880
 names, A and B, and Alice and Bob.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.840
 And then there's some bad guys.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:01.160
 There's the bad guys, and often they

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:05.240
 are called C, like Carol, or Carlos, or Charlie,

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.800
 or something like that.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.120
 They're even Chuck.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:09.720
 Even Chuck is a bad guy.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:12.720
 Or Dave or Eve, Eve for the eavesdropper.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:17.000
 And the idea is somewhere in the middle here,

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.360
 somewhere in the middle, you have

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.280
 some person with bad intent.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.520
 Here we have Trinity from The Matrix,

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:27.680
 and she looks as bad as you can look, right?

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:30.520
 So Alice and Bob seem to be real happy people.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:33.480
 They're just trying to get things done

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.440
 and send some information without being bothered.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.520
 And then Trinity's there eavesdropping.

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:40.440
 But there's other things.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:41.560
 You can eavesdrop.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:44.400
 You can sort of redirect the message and change it.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.720
 There's all kinds of things that the bad guy in the middle

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:47.880
 is going to do.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:51.840
 And so Alice and Bob are far away from each other,

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.340
 and they have to communicate securely.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:57.640
 And it's a literal gauntlet of problems

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:00.040
 that they have to face, and various people

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:03.360
 with bad intent, with bad purposes, sometimes just

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.600
 wanting to see what's going on versus wanting

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:09.320
 to change what's going on versus completely redirect

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:09.920
 communication.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:13.960
 So Alice, Bob, and then a whole series of bad guys

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:18.840
 with various bad guys and gals with various evil intent.

